---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---
<BaseLayout title="Projects - Daksh Verma" description="Engineering case studies - backend systems, AI pipelines, distributed architectures" currentPath="/projects">

<div class="page-header"><div class="container">
  <p class="section-label">Engineering Portfolio</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">Projects</h1>
  <p class="page-desc">Interactive case studies of production-grade systems, AI pipelines, and engineering experiments.</p>
</div></div>

<section class="section" style="padding-top:20px;">
<div class="container">

<article class="case-study reveal" id="finvault">
  <div class="case-study-header">
    <span class="project-card-tier">Tier 1 | Full-Stack + AI | Mar 2026</span>
    <h2 class="case-study-title">FinVault - Agentic Personal Finance Manager</h2>
    <p class="case-study-meta">Privacy-First Mobile Finance Platform</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Problem</h3><p>Existing finance apps require cloud sync of sensitive financial data. Build a privacy-first alternative with AI-powered categorization that can work offline and comply with India's DPDP Act 2023.</p></div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Architecture</h3>
    <div class="arch-diagram">
      <span class="arch-node">Camera/Receipt</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">ML Kit OCR</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">Gemini AI</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">Categorization</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">SecureStore</span>
    </div>
    <p>React Native + Expo Router frontend. Node.js/Express/MongoDB cloud layer with JWT state-protected route validation APIs, local cryptographic container storage via SecureStore, and native OTP verification engines. On-device ML Kit OCR for receipt parsing. Gemini AI for structured JSON categorization. Architecture roadmap includes an unbundled Agentic Commerce Engine across open ONDC network nodes and RxDB/SQLite edge-first topology for zero-latency.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Technologies</h3>
    <div class="project-card-tags"><span class="tag">React Native</span><span class="tag">Expo</span><span class="tag">Node.js</span><span class="tag">MongoDB</span><span class="tag">Gemini AI</span><span class="tag">ML Kit OCR</span><span class="tag">JWT</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Try It Out</h3>
    <div class="project-card-links">
      <a href="https://github.com/i-harshit-sharma/app-dev/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Download APK Release -></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>

<article class="case-study reveal" id="etmarkets">
  <div class="case-study-header">
    <span class="project-card-tier">Tier 1 | GenAI Systems | 2026</span>
    <h2 class="case-study-title">ET Markets AI Intelligence Platform</h2>
    <p class="case-study-meta">The Economic Times GenAI Hackathon 2026 | Team NITDominars</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Problem</h3><p>Indian retail investors struggle to convert fragmented financial data into actionable decisions. The solution requires an intelligence layer that unifies market scanning, charting, AI chat, and video generation.</p></div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Architecture</h3>
    <div class="arch-diagram">
      <span class="arch-node">FastAPI Gateway</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">Radar Engine</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">Chart AI</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">MarketGPT RAG</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">Video Pipeline</span>
    </div>
    <p>Modular-monolith integration approach built on a unified FastAPI Gateway. Houses 4 core engines: Opportunity Radar (signal generation), Chart Pattern Intelligence (technical pattern extraction & confidence scoring), MarketGPT (Portfolio-context Q&A orchestration via RAG), and AI Video Engine (TTS narration synthesis and MP4 rendering). Engineered with asynchronous offloading for long-running video pipelines.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Impact Model</h3>
    <p>Calculated to save an estimated 9.17 hours/month per user via accelerated discovery, yielding an annualized time-value and decision-quality improvement equivalent to INR 40,212 per user. Scaled to 3,500 active users, this projects a ~14 Crore INR annual impact footprint.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Technologies</h3>
    <div class="project-card-tags"><span class="tag">FastAPI</span><span class="tag">Python</span><span class="tag">Groq API</span><span class="tag">RAG</span><span class="tag">TTS Engine</span><span class="tag">yfinance</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Links</h3>
    <div class="project-card-links"><a href="https://github.com/DakshVerma11/ET_GenAI_Hackathon" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub -></a></div>
  </div>
</article>

<article class="case-study reveal" id="aml-pipeline">
  <div class="case-study-header">
    <span class="project-card-tier">Tier 1 | AI + Graph Systems | Sep 2025</span>
    <h2 class="case-study-title">Anti-Money Laundering Neural Pipeline</h2>
    <p class="case-study-meta">National CyberShield Hackathon | MANIT Bhopal | Team NITDominars</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Problem</h3><p>Traditional rule-based AML systems produce excessive false positives and cannot detect complex multi-layered transaction laundering patterns that span networks of shell accounts.</p></div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Architecture</h3>
    <div class="arch-diagram">
      <span class="arch-node">Transactions</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">GAT Model</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">MLP Classifier</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">PageRank</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">Cycle Detection</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">Investigation GUI</span>
    </div>
    <p>Phase 1: Custom 2-layer Graph Attention Network with 3 attention heads and 96 hidden dimensions. Consumes 240-dimensional consolidated embeddings (96-dim source + 96-dim destination + 48-dim transaction features). MLP classifier with explicit batch normalization and 0.4 dropout.</p>
    <p>Phase 2: Suspicious nodes trigger automated 2-hop and 3-hop neighborhood expansions. Personalized PageRank (alpha=0.85) propagates suspicion scores. Deterministic cycle calculations and community detection identify structural laundering loops.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Scale & Metrics</h3>
    <div class="case-metrics">
      <div class="metric"><div class="metric-value">56.4K</div><div class="metric-label">Transactions</div></div>
      <div class="metric"><div class="metric-value">77.6K</div><div class="metric-label">Graph Nodes</div></div>
      <div class="metric"><div class="metric-value">98.91%</div><div class="metric-label">Accuracy</div></div>
      <div class="metric"><div class="metric-value">99.81%</div><div class="metric-label">AUC-ROC</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Technologies</h3>
    <div class="project-card-tags"><span class="tag">PyTorch</span><span class="tag">Graph Attention Networks</span><span class="tag">Neo4j</span><span class="tag">FastAPI</span><span class="tag">PageRank</span></div>
  </div>
</article>

<article class="case-study reveal" id="chatzero">
  <div class="case-study-header">
    <span class="project-card-tier">Tier 1 | Backend Systems | Jun-Jul 2025</span>
    <h2 class="case-study-title">ChatZero - Real-Time Messaging System</h2>
    <p class="case-study-meta">C-DAC Noida | Software Engineering Internship</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Problem</h3><p>Build a production-ready real-time messaging system with strong authentication, persistent chat history, friend management, and background maintenance - all within a monolithic Spring Boot architecture.</p></div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Architecture</h3>
    <div class="arch-diagram">
      <span class="arch-node">Browser</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">Spring Security</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">STOMP Broker</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">WebSocket Handler</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">JPA/Hibernate</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">MySQL</span>
    </div>
    <p>Session-based auth fortified with BCrypt password hashing and Google reCAPTCHA. In-memory STOMP broker for real-time concurrent messaging. Custom cron jobs for background message maintenance and cleanup.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Technologies</h3>
    <div class="project-card-tags"><span class="tag">Java</span><span class="tag">Spring Boot</span><span class="tag">Spring Security</span><span class="tag">WebSockets</span><span class="tag">STOMP</span><span class="tag">JPA/Hibernate</span><span class="tag">MySQL</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Links</h3>
    <div class="project-card-links"><a href="https://github.com/DakshVerma11/ChatZero" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub -></a></div>
  </div>
</article>

<article class="case-study reveal" id="ai-interviewer">
  <div class="case-study-header">
    <span class="project-card-tier">Tier 2 | AI Engineering | Jun 2025</span>
    <h2 class="case-study-title">AI Interviewer Prototype</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Problem</h3><p>Automate interview proctoring with real-time gaze tracking, vocal analysis, and candidate scoring.</p></div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Architecture</h3>
    <div class="arch-diagram">
      <span class="arch-node">Video Feed</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">OpenCV</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">Gaze Tracking</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">Whisper ASR</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">Scoring Engine</span>
    </div>
    <p>Multi-user session isolation with independent background processing threads. Integrates real-time OpenCV tracking modules to compute eye gaze anomalies and spatial integrity/proctoring metrics. Parses candidate vocal recordings through Whisper + PyAnnote audio processing pipelines to calculate words-per-minute distributions, filler-word ratios, lexical relevance metrics, and clarity scores. (Note: Question evaluation currently supported via static placeholders rather than full NLP nodes).</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Technologies</h3>
    <div class="project-card-tags"><span class="tag">React</span><span class="tag">Flask</span><span class="tag">OpenCV</span><span class="tag">Whisper</span><span class="tag">PyAnnote</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Links</h3>
    <div class="project-card-links"><a href="https://github.com/DakshVerma11/AI_Interviewer_Prototype" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub -></a></div>
  </div>
</article>

<article class="case-study reveal" id="gesture-bridge">
  <div class="case-study-header">
    <span class="project-card-tier">Tier 2 | Deep Learning | Mar-May 2025</span>
    <h2 class="case-study-title">Gesture Bridge - Real-Time Sign Language Translator</h2>
    <p class="case-study-meta">NIT Delhi Semester 4 Capstone Project</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Architecture</h3>
    <div class="arch-diagram">
      <span class="arch-node">Camera</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">MediaPipe</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">CNN + Bi-LSTM</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">LLM Translation</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">Multi-Language Output</span>
    </div>
    <p>Bridging communication barriers for the Deaf and Hard-of-Hearing (DHH) community. Real-time ISL interpretation leveraging MediaPipe pipelines to trace coordinate streams for hand/facial landmarks. Structural feeds are processed through an integrated Convolutional Neural Network coupled with a Bidirectional Long Short-Term Memory (CNN + Bi-LSTM) layer for chronological spatial gesture classification. Supports translation to multiple Indian regional languages via an LLM execution link.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Technologies</h3>
    <div class="project-card-tags"><span class="tag">Python</span><span class="tag">TensorFlow</span><span class="tag">MediaPipe</span><span class="tag">OpenCV</span><span class="tag">CNN</span><span class="tag">Bi-LSTM</span></div>
  </div>
</article>

<article class="case-study reveal" id="ecoloop">
  <div class="case-study-header">
    <span class="project-card-tier">Tier 2 | Systems Design | Mid 2025</span>
    <h2 class="case-study-title">EcoLoop - Sustainability Tracking System</h2>
    <p class="case-study-meta">Walmart Sparkathon 2025 | Team NITDominars</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Architecture</h3>
    <div class="arch-diagram">
      <span class="arch-node">IoT Sensors</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">Prediction Engine</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">Dynamic Pricing</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">Blockchain Ledger</span><span class="arch-arrow">-></span>
      <span class="arch-node">EcoScore Dashboard</span>
    </div>
    <p>AI-IoT proactive pricing layer matches on-shelf weight sensors with analytical prediction loops to compute perishable food degradation curves up to 72 hours in advance, triggering automated escalating retail discounts. Circular supply distribution mesh for beverage recycling logged immutably on a distributed blockchain ledger. Engineered a gamified "Earth Coins" tokenized incentive core for sustainable purchase loops.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Technologies</h3>
    <div class="project-card-tags"><span class="tag">IoT</span><span class="tag">ML Prediction</span><span class="tag">Blockchain</span><span class="tag">Supply Chain</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Links</h3>
    <div class="project-card-links"><a href="https://lnkd.in/gBp7efRk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Pitch Video & Architecture -></a></div>
  </div>
</article>

<article class="case-study reveal" id="linearreg">
  <div class="case-study-header">
    <span class="project-card-tier">Tier 2 | Systems Programming | Nov 2023</span>
    <h2 class="case-study-title">LinearReg Billing & Inventory System</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Problem</h3><p>Build a complete enterprise billing and inventory management system in pure C with integrated ML-powered product recommendations.</p></div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Architecture</h3>
    <p>Fully unified command-line enterprise billing and structural storage inventory control platform built with GCC Compiler. Integrates a deterministic machine learning module utilizing historical sales ledgers to fit an internal linear regression model, computing optimized product affinity suggestions at checkout. Outputs structural operational receipts formatted directly into plaintext and PDF schemas.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Technologies</h3>
    <div class="project-card-tags"><span class="tag">C</span><span class="tag">Linear Regression</span><span class="tag">GCC Compiler</span><span class="tag">File I/O</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Links</h3>
    <div class="project-card-links"><a href="https://github.com/DakshVerma11/Billing-Inventory_System_in_C" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub -></a></div>
  </div>
</article>

<article class="case-study reveal" id="prime-pop">
  <div class="case-study-header">
    <span class="project-card-tier">Tier 2 | Mathematical Modeling | 2022</span>
    <h2 class="case-study-title">The Prime Population Research Framework</h2>
    <p class="case-study-meta">Sanskriti School | Shri R. S. Niamat Rai Rajpal Memorial Contest</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Architecture</h3>
    <p>Acted as Core Mathematical Researcher. Gathered, normalized, and parsed metric tracking records across 40 major global cities. Combined Bayesian probabilistic models, structural Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN), and mathematical regression algorithms to formulate multi-variable population density projection equations while systematically minimizing residual errors.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="case-section"><h3>Technologies</h3>
    <div class="project-card-tags"><span class="tag">Bayesian Probabilities</span><span class="tag">CNN</span><span class="tag">Regression Algorithms</span><span class="tag">Data Normalization</span></div>
  </div>
</article>

</div>
</section>

</BaseLayout>
